tlosint-spiderfoot (4.0+git20231105.0f815a2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. SpiderFoot in a dedicated virtualenv under
    /opt/tracelabs/spiderfoot, with hash-pinned dependencies.
  * Version carries a commit stamp because the shipped tree is NOT the v4.0
    tag: upstream's declared version is still 4.0, but this is master as of
    2023-11-05, nineteen months later. Plain "4.0" would claim a release we
    are not shipping. Same convention as whatsmyname -- see handoff section 8.
  * "Tier C" package, following packages/metagoofil: upstream ships neither
    setup.py nor pyproject.toml, so pip cannot install it as a package. The
    virtualenv holds only the pinned dependencies; the upstream tree is
    fetched at build time, verified against the commit SHA and sha256 in
    debian/upstream.pin, and laid down verbatim beside the venv.
  * Ships relaxed dependency pins. Upstream's requirements.txt is a wall of
    2023-era upper bounds that are largely uninstallable on trixie's Python
    3.13; in particular cryptography>=3.4.8,<4 has no cp313 wheel and would
    require a Rust toolchain in the build. The upper bounds are stripped and
    the lower bounds kept, except for PyPDF2 and secure, where relaxing was
    tested and breaks upstream code at runtime. Every divergence is recorded
    in debian/README.Debian.
  * Pinned to post-v4.0 master rather than the v4.0 tag; the reasoning is in
    debian/upstream.pin, which must be read before re-pinning.
  * No systemd unit: sf.py starts a web UI on 127.0.0.1:5001 and whether that
    listens on an analyst workstation is an operator decision.

 -- Trace Labs VM Team <vm-team@tracelabs.org>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
